    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear you but i really dont want to go. i looked it up online and people say that hemiplegic migraines can actually cause facial drooping and speech issues too. if i just take a heavy dose of some migraine meds and rest, can't we just monitor it here for an hour? like, if i take 1200mg of ibuprofen and maybe some alexandrite or something strong, won't that just calm the inflammation and fix the neurological stuff if it's just a migraine? i'm pretty sure i can just manage this at home if it's just an aura.",
